  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an integer array `nums`. In one operation, you can add or subtract 1 from **any** element of `nums`.\n\nOutput the **smallest** number of operations to make all elements of `nums` divisible by 3.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [1,2,3,4]\n\n**Output:** 3\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nAll array elements can be made divisible by 3 using 3 operations:\n\n* Subtract 1 from 1.\n* Add 1 to 2.\n* Subtract 1 from 4.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [3,6,9]\n\n**Output:** 0\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 50`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 50`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
